  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$defs": {
    "City": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "A New Zealand city or town. This is the controlled vocabulary for the location of a workplace: every workplace has an address, and at a minimum that address is a city, so this enum is what makes 'has a city' checkable rather than merely non-empty. MATCHING is case-insensitive and diacritic-insensitive: values are listed without macrons for consistency with the existing members, so 'Whangarei' matches 'Whangarei' and 'Whangarei' spelled with a macron, and 'Otaki' matches 'Otaki' spelled with one. Known spelling variants resolve to the member listed here -- notably 'Wanganui' to 'Whanganui'. Suburbs resolve to their city, so an address in Mount Eden is in Auckland. SCOPE is New Zealand only. An office outside New Zealand cannot be expressed here; set `country` instead and leave the city as free text. This constraint therefore applies when `country` is New Zealand or absent.",
